<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-AI5-WINLINT-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-AI5-WINLINT-003" ;
  triage:title "Windows-only large_enum_variant clippy failure: SendRequestEnvelope::Compose(SendRequest) grew past threshold on windows-latest -- fails just lint on windows-latest" ;
  triage:description "Reported by quality-mgr in AI5-QA-1 verdict (PR #600, run 29787382349): Just lint (windows-latest) failing on a NEW clippy diagnostic (`large_enum_variant`, 'large size difference between variants') distinct from the already-fixed ATM-QA-AI4-WINLINT-001. quality-mgr could not pinpoint file:line locally -- cross-compiling to windows-msvc target for repro is blocked in this environment by a macOS/sqlite3-sys C-toolchain gap (missing Windows CRT headers via Xcode clang), independently reconfirmed by team-lead via two separate cross-compile attempts (workspace-wide and package-scoped), both failing identically on libsqlite3-sys@0.31.0's build script. CI's raw log for the windows-latest lint job also does not retain file:line (only the condensed run_lint.py summary line is present; no log artifact was uploaded -- gh api .../artifacts confirms zero artifacts). Root cause located via source-reading background-agent investigation (compilation-free): crates/atm-core/src/protocol.rs:30, enum `SendRequestEnvelope { Compose(SendRequest), Acknowledge(AckRequest) }`. `SendRequest` (crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs:60) embeds a `to: AgentAddress` field; AI.5's chat-address-identity sprint (commit 17bfb4c0, 'add canonical chat identity parsing') grew `AgentAddress` (crates/atm-core/src/address.rs) from 2 fields (agent, team) to 4 (agent, chat_id, team, host). Measured on macOS (size_of, debug profile): SendRequest = 336 bytes, AckRequest = 144 bytes -> gap = 192 bytes, just under clippy's default 200-byte large_enum_variant threshold, which is why it is silent on macOS/ubuntu. Windows-latest's rustc struct-layout/padding for the String/PathBuf/Option<T> chain in the now-larger struct evidently pushes the gap >=200 bytes, tripping the lint only there. No other enum in crates/atm-core/src/** is nearly this close to the threshold (RequestEnvelope's top-two variants differ by only 16 bytes; everything else is far below). This matches the established repo fix pattern for this exact lint class: task AG14-CI-FIX-WIN-1 (commit ef9aeb31) boxed PersistedAckReply::Sent(SentAckReply) -> Sent(Box<SentAckReply>) for an identical platform-size-dependent large_enum_variant regression." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "QA" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "single_file" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-AI5-WINLINT-003/pAI-6/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-6/545578b0> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-6/545578b0> ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAI-s6-http-uds-router" ;
  triage:resolution "OPEN, dispatch-ready, CI-red-everywhere early-fix exception (blocks windows-latest just lint on PR #600 and will block AI.6's PR). Fix: box the large variant -- change crates/atm-core/src/protocol.rs:30 `SendRequestEnvelope::Compose(SendRequest)` to `Compose(Box<SendRequest>)`. Update the ~4 known construction/match sites: protocol.rs:571 (match, no change needed -- Box derefs transparently in match ergonomics only if using box patterns, otherwise use `.as_ref()` or `**boxed`), protocol.rs:986 (construction -- wrap in `Box::new(..)`), protocol.rs:1007 (match/binding -- adjust to bound `Box<SendRequest>` or deref), transport/testing.rs:72 (match/binding -- same adjustment). arch-ctm must verify against Windows CI, not local macOS lint -- local lint cannot detect this class of bug (confirmed: threshold-adjacent size difference only crosses clippy's 200-byte cutoff under Windows struct layout)." ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-21T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-AI5-WINLINT-003/pAI-6/1>
